  "live_records": {
    "q-32411": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32411",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖$, if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}+6 \\\\ \\frac{s}{s-10} \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}({s}^{2}+6) \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{s-10} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}{e}^{5s}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}({s}^{2}+6) & ={0}^{2}+6=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{s-10} & =\\frac{0}{0-10}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}{e}^{5s} & ={e}^{5(0)}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(s)‖$ as $s$ approaches $0$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖ & =‖{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)‖ \\\\  & =‖[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{37}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
